        <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="/events/2017-08-01-tdd-phpactor-refactoring/"/>
        <id>/events/2017-08-01-tdd-phpactor-refactoring/</id>
        
        <content type="html" xml:base="/events/2017-08-01-tdd-phpactor-refactoring/">&lt;h2 id=&quot;talk-1-tdd-in-action&quot;&gt;Talk 1: TDD in Action&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;History and concepts of TDD; why it is needed; Tools &amp;amp; integration examples. Audience: beginners+intermediate.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;a href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;twitter.com&#x2F;KifahAbbad&quot;&gt;Kifah Abbad&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;talk-2-phpactor-lightweight-refactoring-and-intellisense&quot;&gt;Talk 2: Phpactor: Lightweight refactoring and intellisense&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Phpactor is a console application which works both as a standalone tool offering a Unix way of refactoring and introspecting your code, and as a lightweight intellisense (auto-completion etc.) solution for editors such as VIM.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;a href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;twitter.com&#x2F;dantleech&quot;&gt;Daniel Leech&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
</content>
        
